  "title": "Kourovka problem 14.54 (main)",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Let k(G) denote the number of conjugacy classes of a finite group G. Is it\ntrue that k(G) ⩽ |N | for some nilpotent subgroup N of G? This is true if G is simple;\nbesides, always k(G) ⩽ |S| for some soluble subgroup S ⩽ G.\n                                                               M. W. Liebeck, L. Pyber\n  ∗ No, not always (S. Tertooy, Preprint, 2026,\nhttps://arxiv.org/abs/2606.21404).",
